+The code was tested with MATLAB R2025b. No external data or separately installed third-party MATLAB package is required. MATLAB is proprietary software, must be obtained separately under an appropriate MathWorks license, and is not included in this repository.
+
+The implementation uses MATLAB functions including `pcg`, `eigs`, `delaunayTriangulation`, `convhulln`, and `delaunayn`. The last two use Qhull internally through MATLAB; this repository does not bundle Qhull source code or binaries. The repository license does not relicense MATLAB or software supplied with it. GNU Octave compatibility has not been verified.
+
+The computations reported in the paper were performed on a MacBook Pro with an Apple M5 Max processor and 128 GB of memory.
 
 The full run of `main_2.m` includes a problem with 17,153 degrees of freedom. Its assembly uses a dense auxiliary accumulator of approximately 2.35 GB, and the spectral computations require additional memory. A high-memory machine is therefore recommended. The `quick` mode is intended only to check the installation and does not reproduce the complete paper tables.
 
